Beryllium is a privacy-focused web browser for FreeBSD, built natively from
the Chromium source with a privacy patch set derived from the GPL-3.0 code
of the Helium browser and the ungoogled-chromium patches it includes.

It keeps the bundled uBlock Origin fork, fingerprinting defences and the
other privacy defaults of that patch set, and is being developed toward a
FreeBSD-native process sandbox built on Capsicum. Beryllium is an
independent project and is not affiliated with Helium or imput.
